60,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Looking at the options, Plan A and Plan D offer shared utility. However, Plan B is in a ground-floor hall, which risks the hazardous material delays I found in the older blocks. I lean toward Plan A.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"Plan A addresses shared utility, but we must consider the timetable. Upgrading ventilation in teaching labs likely requires taking them out of service, which could lead to the costly off-site rentals I discovered.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,George,,"Plan A is the only option that directly addresses the operational burden. By upgrading the extraction equipment, we can eliminate the manual routines that are currently draining our technicians' time and energy.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Plan C is far too risky; it's entirely exposed to the weather, and my data shows we lose weeks to rain and frost. Plan A is a necessary upgrade, not just ""appeal,"" making it more likely to stay on schedule.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Plan A is certainly the most pragmatic. While Plan D sounds lovely, my findings on audiovisual reserves suggest we cannot afford its long-term upkeep. Plan A addresses essential infrastructure, which usually commands more realistic budgeting.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Victoria, if we schedule Plan A's work during the summer break, we can mitigate the rental costs. Given the consensus on operational relief and shared utility, Plan A seems the most robust choice.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, summer work helps, but we must ensure the scope doesn't bleed into the term. If we can guarantee the timetable remains intact, Plan A's utility and operational benefits make it the most rational choice.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,George,,"I agree. If we can manage the timing, Plan A is the only choice that provides a sustainable solution for our staff. We cannot continue to rely on manual workarounds for essential equipment.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Victoria, since Plan A is a necessary infrastructure upgrade rather than a ""comfort"" project, it's far less likely to suffer the year-long slips I've seen. It's the most predictable and deliverable option we have.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"It is rare to see such a harmonious alignment of interests. Plan A satisfies the need for utility, staff relief, and predictability, while avoiding the financial void of unreserved AV costs. I find it quite compelling.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"Since we have addressed the concerns regarding timetable disruption and financial risk, and given that Plan A provides both shared utility and operational relief, I see no reason to consider other options. I vote for Plan A.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"I agree. While I remain cautious about the timetable, the collective benefits for staff and students outweigh the risks, provided we manage the schedule strictly. I also vote for Plan A.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,George,,I agree. Plan A is the only proposal that provides a tangible solution to the staffing strain. It is a necessary investment in our people as much as our facilities. I vote for Plan A.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"I agree. Plan A is the most realistic choice. It avoids the weather risks of Plan C and the scheduling pitfalls of ""appeal"" projects. For the sake of stability and predictability, I vote for Plan A.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,It appears the evidence has spoken with an unusual degree of clarity. Plan A is the only option that balances operational necessity with financial realism. I shall join the chorus and vote for Plan A.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"The consensus is absolute. We have weighed the risks of hazardous materials, scheduling slips, and financial reserves, and Plan A emerges as the only viable path forward. I am satisfied with this outcome.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over.""}]}"
76,3,4,pass,Toshio,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
77,3,4,talk,Victoria,,"I am also satisfied. By acknowledging the risks to the timetable and the operational burdens, we have reached a decision that is both pragmatic and sustainable. I concur with the final consensus.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
78,3,4,pass,Victoria,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
79,3,4,talk,George,,I am glad we could reach this agreement. Prioritizing the well-being and efficiency of our staff ensures the long-term success of the university. I am fully satisfied with this decision.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
80,3,4,pass,George,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
81,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,"I am satisfied as well. By prioritizing a necessary upgrade over an optional one, we minimize the risk of delays and ensure a predictable delivery. This is the most responsible choice for everyone.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
82,3,4,pass,Mizuki,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
83,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,It is a rare pleasure to witness a committee reach a unanimous decision without a single dramatic outburst. Plan A is the only logical conclusion. I am satisfied.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
